Never thought about how serius the damage they cause really is have we?

One level of rust equals to one point of Ac for the base protection of a
piece of armor, but it never makes it negative.

Something that gives one point of Ac when undamaged and +0, like an orcish
helm, gets exactly one Ac point worse when it's rusty, very rusty or even
thoroughly rusty. If it is enchanted, it still protects for the value of
its enchantment. Rustproofing it when it is not yet rusty, doesn't give
any better Ac. Repairing it when it has some rust damage gives one point
better Ac. I'd sooner spend that scroll on enchanting it (or something
else), unless everything I wear is already at +4 or better.
When something that gives more base protection than one point gets rusty,
that's another thing.

And rust monsters only damage metal stuff you're wearing or wielding,
doing no harm to yourself. So, when there is nobody else but you and the
rust monster, just take off any rustprone armor and unwield your weapon
before attacking. If it is close to you, take some distance and close a
door or go up/downstairs before taking off the armor.
And often your rustprone helmet or pair of boots is +0 and there is an
equally good one near, so then it doesn't matter whether the helmet gets
cursed or not. 
And most good body armor (mithril, dagon scale mails) doesn't rust anyway.

